{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/683371-what-do-i-need-to-play","id":683371,"title":"What do I need to play?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-30T12:14:43-07:00","id":683371,"title":"What do I need to play?","content":"I'm going to buy the vampire the requiem rulebook soon. What else will I need besides friends to play with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T12:26:36-07:00","id":683428,"title":"","content":"If you're getting the 1st edition rule book, you'll also need the base World of Darkness rule book too. If you're getting the 2nd edition rule book, you don't need any other books, just lots of 10-sided dice. <br /> <br /> Some extra non-essential, but still useful things to have: Index cards are great for tracking various things like Conditions or other temporary effects. I like having some of those flat-bottom colored glass bead things to keep track of Willpower, Vitae, and Beats instead of constantly erasing and re-writing on the character sheets. If you're playing 2nd Edition, the God-Machine Chronicle has some Merits and stuff that aren't in VtR2e. The rules update chapter is free in PDF format on drivethruRPG. Damnation City is a great supplement for either edition, as is Blood Sorcery: Sacriments and Blasphemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T12:31:19-07:00","id":683434,"title":"","content":"Thanks! A second question, does the rulebook explain how to actually run a game in terms of storyline/characters/ etc or will we provide that sort of stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T13:27:41-07:00","id":683466,"title":"","content":"There is a section on Storytelling advice, but like with any roleplaying game, you'll ultimately have to lay some groundwork of your own. 2e has a fantastic section for building character ties called &quot;climbing the ladder&quot; that I've found incredibly helpful in pupulating a setting with NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:32:59-07:00","id":683602,"title":"","content":"A big endorsement for Damnation City. It's damn near the perfect tool for creating your own city or modifying an existing one to suit your game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T16:09:39-07:00","id":683623,"title":"","content":"I would recommend WoD 1e and God Machine Chronicles both even if you have the 2e book. There were numerous situations I had with my group when I ran that just weren't covered by 2e alone. Just be aware that a WoD 2e book is coming out eventually that may make the other two obsolete.<br /> <br /> That said, I've done just fine with WoD core, GMC, and VtR 2e. GMC mostly just words a few rules a little different such that it can help if you're unsure what a rule in VtR means. Also slightly expanded combat via introducing Tilts and a lot more Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T16:53:38-07:00","id":683642,"title":"","content":"I recommend against buying the God Machine Chronicles book, as the World of Darkness 2e rulebook has been said to incorporate it. Instead, you can just download the rules update part of the book for free! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">[LINK]</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T18:48:04-07:00","id":683703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xizzicks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/683371-what-do-i-need-to-play#post683371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to buy the vampire the requiem rulebook soon. What else will I need besides friends to play with?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Core book for basic rules and Requiem book for rules on playing vampire. That's about it, other books in the series are just supplements to add more flavor to the game. As for advice on story telling, the Requiem book gives a few examples of potential enemies (Gargoyles, Hormunculi, Hell Hounds and Rogue Ghouls) and provides a basic story introduction set in New Orleans with NPC's already written up in the book. You just need to think of a story, write up some PC's and play it out. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-30-2015, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}